from release_tools import package
package('V1.12.0','''# V1.12.0 — Retailer Input Files

Enhances V1.11.A1. Retailer Setup has an Input Files tab with multiple separately saved Transaction or Master Product inputs. Each input has Delimiter, Encoding, Type of File, isZipFolder, Sheet Password, Filename, File Path, Max Columns and 1-based Header Row settings, plus its own sample upload smaller than 1 MB and first-25-row preview. Input settings appear in configuration history and accepted batch metadata. Save Configuration retains input definitions. Rules are still shared by retailer; Use Sample in Rules previews the chosen input's sample, and final-example export uses that sample.

Read modes are Manual and Automatic. Read From Path reads a saved file or a folder's single matching filename/pattern, runs backend preprocessing and starts a batch for the editable ISO week. Automatic watches the configured path every 1, 5 or 15 minutes while the app runs, requires two stable scans and an unchanged read, and uses the current Malaysia ISO week. It skips previously accepted unchanged content for the same profile/path, including after restart, and records recent accepted/blocked delivery details. Changed content creates a fresh run. Preprocessing failures can be retried after setup changes; actual execution failures retain their own cancelled log rows and need manual reprocessing. Archive disables automatic reads and rejects manual reads. This is an app-lifetime watcher, not a Windows scheduled service. The DATAFLOW_WATCH_ENABLED=0 environment option disables background watching for tests/deployment.

File reads are confined to Codex, following the user's access rule. Full file paths and folder paths with filename wildcards are supported. CSV, TSV and Text use explicit delimiter/encoding; JSON uses named keys and Header Row 1. Excel reads the first worksheet. ZIP is read in memory without extraction, supports one member of the configured type, and enforces bounded size and safe entry names. Batch input is at most 50 MB; each sample and its uncompressed ZIP member are smaller than 1 MB. Samples support up to 10,000 rows and profiles up to 1,000 columns. Parsing settings/password revisions make existing samples stale until reuploaded.

Sheet Password is for encrypted Excel workbooks; worksheet protection alone permits reading and needs no password. Excel decryption uses msoffcrypto-tool. Passwords are protected with Windows DPAPI under the current Windows user, stored separately in SQLite, and never returned by API or included in configuration history or GitHub. Keep, replace and clear actions are supported. Encrypted ZIP archives are not supported.

Data Streams offers saved Input File Settings for uploads and applies the selected parser in preprocessing, launch and reprocessing. Accepted parsed rows are privately captured for in-flight execution, so later parser/password edits cannot alter an already accepted run. The temporary parsed-row cache is deleted on finalization. Reprocessing uses the latest saved input profile and rules; removed profiles require a fresh upload with current settings. Previous-week file-size comparisons use the same input profile, keeping Transaction and Master Product baselines separate. No batch data preview is added to audit logs.

Readiness checks every input's saved sample/settings and reports missing/stale samples or schema issues. Legacy retailer samples/uploads remain supported for earlier setups. The single outputs/V1.3.A1.bat launcher opens V1.12.0 at http://127.0.0.1:5001/. Close the old server window and reopen this launcher. Existing local SQLite data is preserved through backup. Databases, samples, encrypted secrets, personal config, dependencies and generated builds are excluded from GitHub.
''','Production Vite build and 106 backend tests passed. Input tests verify separate samples and rule previews, stale settings, DPAPI secret privacy, encrypted Excel read/password clearing, ZIP traversal/column bounds, JSON and upload limits, captured parsing and reprocessing, stable/new/unchanged watcher reads, archive blocking, path scope, invalid settings, deletion cleanup, per-input readiness and separate previous-week baselines. Existing history, comparison, audit, store and batch tests passed. Interactive browser verification was not performed.\n',launcher=True)
